A mount fills a table slot of the caller's own process rather than of the process it was invoked on,
so a capability to one process changes what another names.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call mounted a table in a process its caller could not control

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@ static int op_process(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap,
         if (err != KERR_OK) {
             return err;
         }
-        return process_mount(proc, arg[1], &tc, slot_node(t, arg[2]));
+        return process_mount(thread_process(t), arg[1], &tc, slot_node(t, arg[2]));
     }
     case OP_PROCESS_UNMOUNT:
         return process_unmount(proc, arg[1]);
